  "metadata": {
    "alignment": "unspecified",
    "description": "tonyd2wild's single-Spark vLLM TP1 profile for NVIDIA's own nvidia/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVFP4 checkpoint, used byte for byte (124 GB; 125B-A6B hybrid MoE, MTP head). The 47.7 GiB per-layer-embedding (n-gram) table stays on the NVMe and only the 16 rows each token needs are read on demand (disk-backed table patch, staged gather so decode runs as CUDA graphs), with a reduced-vocabulary MTP draft (65,536 ids), MTP 3, FP8 KV, memory utilization 0.80, 262,144 context, six sequences and 4,096-token prefill chunks (upstream defaults). The adapter bakes upstream's patch files and its vLLM overlays (PR #55375 fused PLE state-index fix, PR #54846 FP8/NVFP4 KV on the QSA path, and two ModelOpt MTP-loading fixes) into the image at upstream's exact vLLM commit 8a728663. Image note: upstream ran the vllm/vllm-openai nightly-8a728663 tag, which is no longer on Docker Hub; the same commit survives only as the cu129-nightly-8a728663 build, which this recipe pins by digest (CUDA 12.9 runtime instead of upstream's CUDA 13), so a Spark start is unverified. The disk-backed table needs the model files on a local NVMe (random reads over NFS crawl). Licences (information only): repository Apache-2.0; vLLM Apache-2.0; checkpoint under the NVIDIA Open Model License and the Qwen licence of the base model. Upstream figures (43.9 tok/s median single stream, 68.8 tok/s aggregate at six streams) are claims until measured here; alternatives from other creators: MiaAI-Lab's single-Spark vLLM and TensorFold kits. Vonk physical Spark acceptance is pending.",
    "tags": [
      "multimodal",
      "mtp",
      "nvfp4",
      "qwen3.8",
      "reasoning",
      "single",
      "spark",
      "tool-use",
